-- Replace zero dates with NULL so the schema can run under a strict sql_mode.
--
-- The dump declares 24 columns as `NOT NULL DEFAULT '0000-00-00 00:00:00'` and
-- another 11 date columns as NOT NULL with no default at all. '0000-00-00' is
-- not a real date: MariaDB only tolerates it with NO_ZERO_DATE removed from
-- sql_mode, and PHP renders it as 01 January 1970, which is what the news
-- listing was showing for undated entries.
--
-- Runs after 02-modernize-schema.sql on a fresh volume, and is idempotent.
--
-- `on update current_timestamp()` is preserved where it exists, and columns
-- that already default to current_timestamp() keep that default — only the
-- zero-date defaults are replaced with NULL.

-- Widen the NOT NULL date columns to accept NULL.
